      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely, let's tackle this zoning conundrum with a strategy that incorporates a few clever tricks, much like a clever goblin might navigate through a labyrinth of traps. First, gather all the relevant documents, including the current zoning map, the municipal code, and any records of the encroachments. Then, consult with a land-use attorney who can help you interpret the code and identify any potential loopholes or precedents that might work in your favor. \n\nNext, consider reaching out to the neighboring property owner to discuss the encroachments. Sometimes, a friendly goblin can negotiate a truce, and in this case, it might mean agreeing to a boundary adjustment or a compromise that satisfies both parties. If that doesn't work, you may need to prepare for a variance application, which will require demonstrating that the existing setbacks are unduly burdensome and that your proposed Mixed-Use development will not negatively impact the surrounding area.\n\nRemember, just like a goblin's cunning can often lead to unexpected treasures, a well-crafted rezoning application can open up new opportunities for your client's parcel. Good luck, and may your efforts be as successful as a goblin's heist!",
